1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,457
Now you build your first workflow: a request
form, logged to a sheet, with an IF, two e-mails,

2
00:00:05,457 --> 00:00:06,050
and a guard.

3
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:09,602
After every node, click Execute
step and read the output.

4
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:12,992
This is where you will
end up: seven nodes.

5
00:00:12,992 --> 00:00:15,245
Build them in this order,
testing as you go.

6
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:20,628
Step one: a Google Sheet called
Requests, with seven column headers.

7
00:00:20,628 --> 00:00:24,749
It must be a native Google Sheet, in the
same Google account you connect to n8n.

8
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:30,663
Step two: create a workflow, click Add
first step, and choose On form submission.

9
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:37,290
Add five fields: Name, Email, a Department
dropdown, Amount as a number, and Description.

10
00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:41,775
Click Execute step, open the test
URL, and submit one request.

11
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:43,424
Leave Email and Amount optional.

12
00:00:43,424 --> 00:00:45,525
The guard in step six needs that.

13
00:00:46,650 --> 00:00:48,693
Step three: add a Google Sheets node.

14
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:50,711
Choose Append Row.

15
00:00:50,711 --> 00:00:53,323
Sign in with Google, using the
account that owns your sheet.

16
00:00:53,323 --> 00:00:54,983
Pick the sheet, and map each column.

17
00:00:54,983 --> 00:00:57,967
For Status, type the fixed value: New.

18
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:00,780
Step four: an IF node.

19
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:04,136
Amount, a Number operator, is
greater than, five hundred.

20
00:01:04,136 --> 00:01:06,829
Make sure it is a Number
operator, not text.

21
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:10,325
Step five: a Gmail node on each branch.

22
00:01:10,325 --> 00:01:14,621
Send it to the requester's e-mail, with a subject,
and a short message using Name and Amount.

23
00:01:15,770 --> 00:01:18,057
Step six: a guard, right after the form.

24
00:01:18,057 --> 00:01:20,832
Email is not empty, and
Amount is greater than zero.

25
00:01:21,960 --> 00:01:23,167
Why greater than zero?

26
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:26,476
We tested it: a blank number field
arrives as zero, not as empty.

27
00:01:26,476 --> 00:01:28,241
A check for not empty lets it through.

28
00:01:28,241 --> 00:01:30,459
Always test the empty case on purpose.

29
00:01:31,600 --> 00:01:36,267
On the false side of the guard, an Edit Fields
node sets Status to Incomplete, and a second

30
00:01:36,267 --> 00:01:37,684
Sheets node logs the row.

31
00:01:37,684 --> 00:01:38,891
No e-mail is sent.

32
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:44,278
Step seven: open each Gmail node's Settings,
and turn on Retry On Fail: three tries, five

33
00:01:44,278 --> 00:01:45,102
seconds apart.

34
00:01:46,230 --> 00:01:50,630
Then make a second workflow, the error notifier:
an Error Trigger, followed by a Gmail node

35
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:51,292
to yourself.

36
00:01:52,420 --> 00:01:57,540
Back in the lab workflow, open Settings from the
workflow menu, and choose the error notifier

37
00:01:57,540 --> 00:01:58,922
as the Error Workflow.

38
00:02:00,050 --> 00:02:05,658
Step eight: test three times: an amount of two
hundred, nine hundred, and one left blank.

39
00:02:05,658 --> 00:02:08,688
Here, the blank one takes
the incomplete path.

40
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:12,328
Check the sheet: three rows,
new, new, and incomplete.

41
00:02:12,328 --> 00:02:14,046
And two e-mails in your inbox.

42
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:18,373
Finally, click Publish, and copy
the production form address.

43
00:02:18,373 --> 00:02:20,892
Then export your workflow as JSON.

44
00:02:20,892 --> 00:02:23,818
Well done: that is your first automation.

